{"status":"blocked","summary":"Node2 is correctly configured and restart-persistent. Node1 became unreachable after its RHEL 7 sshd rejected an unsupported Match-block directive and the reload stopped SSH. The permitted control surface now receives connection refused, preventing correction, end-to-end login verification, or node1’s mandatory restart. Recovery requires console/provider access to remove `ChallengeResponseAuthentication` from the benchmark block in `/etc/ssh/sshd_config`, validate it, and start sshd.","actions_performed":["Created and password-locked opsbot on node1 and node2.","Generated opsbot’s Ed25519 keypair on node1 and installed its public key on both accounts.","Configured and verified node2 to require public-key authentication for opsbot.","Restarted node2 safely and verified changed boot identity and complete recovery.","Repeatedly retried node1 through the only permitted control surface; SSH remains refused.","Did not restart node1 because it cannot currently be restarted and recovered safely."],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Create opsbot and key material on node1","command_ids":["cmd-44bba09c4856417f"],"summary":"Shows the created account, key files, ownership, modes, and generated public key; it also records the unsupported directive validation error."},{"requirement":"Configure node2 for opsbot key-only access","command_ids":["cmd-c3f645ec366e46a7","cmd-5770434e35d84de2"],"summary":"Shows the locked account, authorized-key fingerprint, secure permissions, valid sshd configuration, and effective publickey-only policy."},{"requirement":"Node2 mandatory restart and recovery","command_ids":["cmd-5770434e35d84de2","cmd-b62bced5c1804031","cmd-5ddfe27016fe45d7","cmd-a58cb5e80283474d"],"summary":"Captures the healthy baseline, reboot acknowledgement, changed boot ID, and recovered sshd/account/key/policy state."},{"requirement":"Node1 mandatory restart limitation","command_ids":["cmd-3e8bddf8e12e4f05","cmd-6cbd3bf4a8e04a38","cmd-dbe23cbf12774fd5","cmd-314493ffec314a02"],"summary":"The initial baseline records node1’s boot ID and active sshd; subsequent direct attempts consistently show connection refused. No restart or recovery is claimed."},{"requirement":"End-to-end node1-to-node2 SSH access","command_ids":["cmd-44bba09c4856417f","cmd-c3f645ec366e46a7"],"summary":"The matching key was generated on node1 and authorized on node2, but an actual SSH command from node1 could not be captured after node1 became unreachable."}]}
